From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan <ryan@esterlines.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 18:38:15 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add xenon-ublock's engine patches to the Ladybird patch
 series

Ladybird's content blocker handles network filters and plain cosmetic
filters, which leaves out much of what uBlock Origin's lists rely on.
These six patches, from xenon-ublock's engine/patches, add the rest:

- 0004: trusted lists and uBlock Origin's resources (scriptlets and
  redirect surrogates), sent to every WebContent process, and the
  adblock crate's css-validation feature
- 0005: $redirect surrogates, $removeparam, and $method
- 0006: scriptlets (##+js) and procedural and action cosmetic filters
  (:has-text(), :upward(), :remove(), ...), run at document start in
  every document, about:blank frames and popups included
- 0007: $popup filters
- 0008: CNAME uncloaking: RequestServer reports a host that DNS shows to
  be an alias, and WebContent's blocker decides
- 0009: an element picker, and a Block Element... context menu action

They come after Xenon's own patches. Most touch some of the same files
(main fetch, ResourceLoader, Document, LibWebView's Application and
WebContentPage, WebContent's ConnectionFromClient and IPC endpoints),
but in other places, so they apply on top of Xenon's without conflicts.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
